There's a security hole in GREATs netfd networking server. Unauthorized
people might get root permissions and are able to retrieve, edit or
delete _all_ files. Only systems without shadow-password are affected.

If you have a system with passwords stored in /etc/passwd please
disable the GREAT netfd server. If you need a shadow library for
using shadow passwords, please let us know. We will send you a
small but working libshadow upon request. 

We will release a fixed version of netfd within the next days.

Sorry. GREAT is still BETA software ;-)

Michaela


